WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome home!
-Thank you. Are you sick of me?

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.667
-I am not -- I want you --
This should be, like, your home.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:07.000
I love that -- I just --
We are big fans of you here.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.100
But you always go for it.
And thank you so much

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.767
for being here.
You look fantastic.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.100
Happy holidays.
-Thank you so much. You too.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.767
-I want to talk to you about
"Jingle Bell Rock."

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.667
But I want to talk to you
about your first group.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:21.701
I didn't know
you were in a group.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.934
-[ Laughs ] Well, I mean,
it wasn't a group.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.400
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.701
-But it was like -- My cousins
and I had a little girl band.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.100
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.067
We didn't perform --
You want the name?

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.767
-Yeah, of course
I know the name.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.234
I want to hear the whole story.
-Oh, my gosh, yeah.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.167
-I want to know the story --
the history about The Lilacs.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.734
-Yes!
-[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:41.634
The Lilacs was, like, a group
that my cousins and I formed.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.801
Then we like --
We performed very small venues.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.901
Just, like, you know,
my living room,

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.601
my family's living room.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.000
-Oh, wow, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.834
-Those two living rooms.
-Yeah, we had no recordings.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:54.100
It was strictly live music.
And, yeah, so we had --

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.167
-What type of music
was The Lilacs?

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.834
-It was like -- like pop.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:00.133
Like, singer-songwriter pop.
Some rap even.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:03.334
It was, like, very expansive.
Yeah, it was really --

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.100
Yeah, versatile.
-How many cousins?

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.000
How many people in your family
was involved?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.367
-It was me and then
my three other cousins.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.634
So it was four of us.
It was a group of four.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.367
-Wow.
-Very eclectic group.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:16.734
We had one -- one, like,
big single or something.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.167
-Do you remember
what your single was?

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:21.033
-Yeah. It was called
"We Are The Lilacs."

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.200
-[ Laughter ]
-It was, like, to introduce --

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.334
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.234
-The album was
the same title, of course.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:27.868
-Yeah. Did you make an album?

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.334
-We made a fake album.
So we, like -- We, like,

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.667
skinned, like, a CD
that was already existing.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:34.434
And we, like, put, like, a --
We made one --

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:35.934
like, a cover
out of construction paper.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.601
-And drawing?
-Yeah, we didn't have a CD.

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.434
But we thought it was, like,
the coolest thing.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.300
We're like, "We have an album.
This is so cool."

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.734
But there were
no recordings of it.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.467
-"We Are The Lilacs."
-"We Are The Lilacs." Yeah.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:48.400
♪ We are The Lilacs,
and together we are one ♪

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.200
♪ We can do anything ♪

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.501
♪ So come on,
let's have some fun ♪

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.567
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow! You know it!

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.400
You know it.
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.634
-Do I -- Yeah, exactly.
Now, did they have --

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.868
The Lilacs --
did they have a big break-up?

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:03.534
Or did they have a...?
-No, actually.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.200
Technically we're, like, still,
I guess, kind of ongoing.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.767
'Cause we never had a break-up.
It's like the longest --

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.434
-Running female group
of all time.

00:02:10.434 --> 00:02:12.033
-Of all time. Yeah.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.701
-Well, if they ever want
to come back

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.200
together and reunite
on our show,

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.167
we would love to have
The Lilacs come on our show.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:21.000
-Oh, my God. Thank you.
Absolutely. We would love that.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.234
By popular demand.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.667
-Yeah, but --
When you were first

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:27.200
starting out,
probably pre-Lilacs,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.100
you didn't want to sing
for anyone.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.234
You were too shy.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.367
That was, like, ongoing
for a really long time.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.834
-Even your mom and everybody?

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.934
-Yeah, my mom, my parents.
It was, like, a whole thing.

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:39.868
I remember the first time
I sang for my mom,

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.367
which was the first time
I sang for anybody.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.734
I, like, made her turn around,
close her eyes.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:46.701
And then I went into my shoe
closet and closed the door.

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.367
It was the only way
I would sing for her.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.434
And everyone had to close their
eyes, like, on the outside,

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:51.767
even though I was in the closet.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.300
-And then she just --
Your mom would be like,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.734
"Okay, I'm just going
to listen to you"?

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.067
Or "I'm going to support this"?
-Yeah.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.300
She was the one who, like,
kind of -- not pushed me,

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.801
because I always
wanted to do it.

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.100
But she knew I that I was shy,
but that I wanted to.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.300
So she would kind of nudge me
at, like, family gatherings

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.901
being like, "Why don't you,
you know, sing something?"

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.000
-Yeah.
-So, I feel like -- Yeah.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.100
She was very --
She played a huge role

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.300
in getting me out there,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.334
which was nice.
-And now here you are.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:15.701
You're not only singing,
but you're also acting.

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.334
But I want to talk about
"Jingle Bell Rock,"

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.400
first of all. Congrats.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.334
Can we play a little bit
of Alessia Cara's

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:21.701
"Jingle Bell Rock"?

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.467
-♪ Jingle bell, jingle bell,
jingle bell rock ♪

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:26.100
-Just puts you
in a good mood, right?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.067
That's on Amazon Music
right now.

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.968
Why "Jingle Bell Rock"?

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:32.200
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you very much.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.167
Well, 'cause, I mean,
I tend to, like, gravitate

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.100
towards, like, super
melancholic songs, you know?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.200
And Christmas songs tend
to be, like, a little bit sad.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.300
But this one -- It felt like
it was really jolly and happy.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.934
And it's kind of
what we all need.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:45.534
But also the real reason,
secretly, that I wanted to it

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.100
is because I wanted
to sing the line,

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.501
"Giddy-up, jingle horse."

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.267
'Cause --

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.834
-It just makes you laugh?
-It makes me laugh.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:52.934
Like, what is a jingle horse?

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.400
I have no idea.
-I have no idea, yeah.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.534
But giddy-up.
Hey, jingle horse, let's go!

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.000
Yeah. No one knows what that is.
-Yeah.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.367
What is a jingle --
I don't know.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.267
-Let's just have fun.
But you're going to be on NBC's

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.667
"A Christmas
in Rockefeller Center,"

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:03.934
that special,
with all of these --

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.267
-Yeah!
-Harry Connick Jr.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:07.434
I mean, it's a big deal.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.934
Will you be performing
"Jingle Bell Rock"?

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.300
-Yes, I will.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.267
And my own Christmas song,
"Make It To Christmas," as well,

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.167
which is really exciting.
-I mean -- Wow.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.400
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-I love it.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.701
Not only do you like
Christmas music,

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.367
but you also like
Christmas movies.

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:23.067
You sent me a very cute photo,
which I love.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.601
-I had to send you this.
-It's so cute.

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:28.400
This is your dog Cleo
watching my special

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.167
"Five More Sleeps"
the other night.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.267
-Yeah. Look at her.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.334
This is literally
like two nights ago.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:34.701
She was fascinated by the dog.

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:36.334
That just goes to show
how good the animation is.

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:38.367
'Cause she thought it was real.
-Thought it was a real dog.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:39.601
-Yeah. It was so cute.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.367
My dad was just watching it,
like, for leisure.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.868
He loves you,
so he was, like, watching it.

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.300
And she was, like, fascinated.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.767
-That's so cute.
Thank you for this.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.934
-So I had to send you that.
No problem. It's so cute.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.534
-I almost want you
to sign this one.

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:51.434
Let's talk about
"Yearly Departed."

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:55.100
This will be on Amazon
Prime Video next month.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.100
They've done this --
They did this last year.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.968
Can you explain a little
about what it is

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.868
and how you were involved?
-Yeah.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.501
So "Yearly Departed" --
Yeah, like you said,

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:04.133
it's the second year
that they're doing this.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.667
And it's basically
like a show that's sort of

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:09.000
like a memorial
for the year prior.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.434
Almost like you're attending
a funeral of the year

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.067
that has passed, you know?
-Yes.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.567
-It's like, you know --
There's some comedic relief.

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:18.067
It's very funny. There's,
like, great female comedians.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.467
All female cast.
-Chelsea Peretti, I love.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.534
-Yeah, and Jane Fonda,
which was incredible.

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.400
Like, so cool.
-Jane Fonda's in --

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.167
-Yeah, she's in this!
This is wild.

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.234
Yeah, so you kind of just --
Everyone gets a moment to speak

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:29.434
and we just, like, talk
about the year that passed

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:31.567
and all the things that died
in the last year.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.400
-Did you get to hang out
with Jane Fonda?

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.067
-No. I didn't.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.133
-[ Laughter ]
-I know. I didn't.

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:38.601
-She's so cool.
-She's the coolest ever.

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:40.133
But, like, I kind of
didn't really get to

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.868
meet a lot of the people
'cause you're kind of --

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.734
It's in a setting,
like a church setting.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:45.501
So you're in pews,
so you just kind of

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.100
see the back
of everybody's heads.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.534
-How was the back
of Jane Fonda's head?

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:50.167
-Wonderful.
-Yeah. It's the coolest.

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:51.834
-Yeah, the coolest.
-It's Jane Fonda.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:52.934
-Yeah. The coolest.

00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:54.501
-I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.400
Here's Alessia Cara
in "Yearly Departed."

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.634
Take a look at this.

00:05:57.634 --> 00:06:00.267
-I am going to vow
to stay hydrated.

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.567
Hello. Moisturized.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.367
And apparently BFFs
with Jane Fonda,

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:05.934
'cause she looks amazing.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:09.033
-[ Cheers ]
-I'm gonna relax.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.667
-I'm gonna be rich and married!

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:13.968
-And I'm gonna go
platinum again.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:16.367
-Oh, my gosh. Alessia Cara?

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:18.834
-Hey, Avon.
Love all of this.

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:21.000
-Girl, we're about to do
an in memoriam.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.000
You have to sing.
-Yeah!

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.934
-No -- No.
I wouldn't want to...intrude.

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:27.467
-Mnh-mnh. Stop it. I insist.

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:29.133
-No -- I really -- I couldn't.

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:30.601
-Girl, I ain't gonna beg you.

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:32.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:34.300
-Cut to --
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.133
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Alessia Cara, everybody!

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:39.267
"Yearly Departed" comes to
Prime Video December 23rd.

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:42.033
You can stream her cover
of "Jingle Bell Rock"

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:43.801
now on Amazon Music.

